  "notes": "A 2 kg autogyro: free-spinning teetering rotor on a mast raked 9 degrees back, a pusher propeller, and a small electric pre-rotator that spins the head up before the takeoff roll and then drops out - the rotor is UNPOWERED in flight, kept turning entirely by the airflow (PLAN Phase 4). Control is cyclic on the free head plus a rudder on the fin, like the full-size machines. Nothing in the engine knows what an autogyro is; the mast rake and the free shaft are the whole trick.\n\nEXPORT NOTES — contact spring numbers are Flightline-typical, not converted — the two contact models differ. drag CdA per axis estimated from the drag parts (x, 2x, 3x). prerotator (3 A) read as a pre-rotator, not a drive. head speed om0 set to 65 rad/s (typical for autorotation), not derived. 1 forward prop(s) exported as thrusters (Tmax estimated); differential yaw where they sit off-centre. fin's rudder exported as a yaw vane (k 0.6 assumed).",
